 ## [Unreleased]
 
 ### Added
-- `network/report-dashboard.py`: a **Posture** page (status tiles, a host × check-group matrix scored PASS/(PASS+FAIL+WARN) with ERR never counted as a pass, and every check across hosts with failing hosts and KB test/fix guidance); a **Posture card** on each host page (checks grouped by area, status chips, domain membership); a **Domain posture** table on the Active Directory page (one canonical status per domain check, the `conflict:` note, and every observer's own status). AD findings now show the domain that host posture established for their host. They sit under a "Confirmed domain context" callout, and only unmapped findings keep the "Uncorrelated signals" caveat. Posture relay and credential findings are filed by their KB check group. Quarantined `POSTURE` lines appear in Run health. Domain-scope findings never create a host row or a host page.
-- `network/bulk-enum-linux.sh` + `network/bulk-enum-windows.py`: `--with-posture` runs the host-posture collector after the privesc enum in the same session; output stays in `linenum.txt`/`winenum.txt`, and the combined payload is saved as `_payload.sh`/`_payload.ps1` in the output dir. Linux runs the privesc body as `( … ) </dev/null`, so nothing in it can read the rest of the stream and an `exit` cannot skip posture. Windows runs each script as its own base64-carried script block on a single line (5.1-safe `param()`, no reliance on how `powershell -Command -` buffers multi-line input). `bulk-enum-windows.py --ad` (requires `--with-posture`) passes `-AdChecks`. The default payloads are unchanged.
-- `network/report.py`: **posture ingestion** — `POSTURE|<id>|<status>|<detail>` lines in host enum output are parsed by a strict anchored parser (`split("|", 3)`, so a `|` inside the detail can never add a field) and bypass the regex rules (no double grading). FAIL/WARN become findings at the KB check's `sev_fail`/`sev_warn` with `kb_match="rule"` and full guidance; every status (incl. PASS/NA/ERR) is recorded per host in a new `posture.json` (`schema_version "1"`) and summarised under `summary.posture`. Domain (`AD-*`) checks are aggregated across observers into **one canonical finding per domain** (`scope="domain"`, `observed_from` list) with a determined-beats-undetermined lattice (FAIL>WARN>PASS>INFO, then ERR, then NA) and a `conflict:` note when observers disagree; domain findings never count toward a host verdict. Malformed, unknown-id, duplicate, or untagged domain lines are **quarantined** (`posture_quarantine` in `findings.json`, stderr warning) without marking the report partial. `--redact` scrubs posture details, observers, and domain names.
