-- `standalones/windows/Invoke-HostPosture.ps1`: read-only **Windows host-posture collector** (PowerShell 5.1-safe, pure ASCII) — 41 host checks (patch age, firewall profiles, Defender RTP/tamper/signatures, BitLocker, Secure Boot, SMBv1 and SMB signing, LLMNR/NBT-NS/WPAD, LDAP client signing, anonymous restrictions, PowerShell v2/logging/language mode, RDP+NLA, LSA PPL/Credential Guard/WDigest/LM compat/LM hash/cached logons, UAC, AlwaysInstallElevated, admins/Guest, AutoLogon (value never printed), LAPS, Spooler, WinRM transport, domain join) in the `POSTURE|…` contract. `-AdChecks` opts in to 15 **domain-posture checks** (password/lockout policy, krbtgt age, Kerberoastable/AS-REP/unconstrained-delegation accounts, adminCount, recursive Domain Admins, Protected Users, MachineAccountQuota, functional level, LDAP signing, trusts, LAPS schema) via bounded, paged (1000), time-limited read-only LDAP against the host's own DC; every AD line is tagged `domain=<dns> observer=<host>`. Without `-AdChecks` no directory query is issued (AD-* report `NA`); off Windows every check reports `NA`.
+- `standalones/windows/Invoke-HostPosture.ps1`: read-only **Windows host-posture collector** (PowerShell 5.1-safe, pure ASCII) — 41 host checks (patch age, firewall profiles, Defender RTP/tamper/signatures, BitLocker, Secure Boot, SMBv1 and SMB signing, LLMNR/NBT-NS/WPAD, LDAP client signing, anonymous restrictions, PowerShell v2/logging/language mode, RDP+NLA, LSA PPL/Credential Guard/WDigest/LM compat/LM hash/cached logons, UAC, AlwaysInstallElevated, admins/Guest, AutoLogon (value never printed), LAPS, Spooler, WinRM transport, domain join) in the `POSTURE|…` contract. `-AdChecks` opts in to 15 **domain-posture checks** (password/lockout policy, krbtgt age, Kerberoastable/AS-REP/unconstrained-delegation accounts, adminCount, recursive Domain Admins, Protected Users, MachineAccountQuota, functional level, LDAP signing, trusts, LAPS schema) via bounded, paged (1000), time-limited read-only LDAP against the host's own DC; every AD line is tagged `domain=<dns> observer=<host>`, including the `NA` (ConstrainedLanguage) and `ERR` (RootDSE unreachable) lines, and RootDSE is read through the same time-limited searcher. A registry read that fails (access denied, provider error) reports `ERR` instead of the absent-value default; LDAP signing passes only when signing **and** channel binding are both enforced. Without `-AdChecks` no directory query is issued (AD-* report `NA`); off Windows every check reports `NA`.
 - `standalones/linux/host-posture.sh`: read-only **Linux host-posture collector** — 43 hardening checks (patching, kernel sysctls, LSM/firewall, sshd effective config incl. `Include` globs, accounts/sudo, sensitive-file modes, mounts, PATH, cron, logging, time sync, Secure Boot, failed units, docker socket, AD-join/keytab) emitted one per line as strict `POSTURE|<check-id>|<PASS|FAIL|WARN|INFO|NA|ERR>|<detail>`; `ERR` (e.g. unreadable as non-root) is never reported as `PASS`. No writes, no network; hermetic test root via `ARANUM_POSTURE_ROOT`. Body runs inside a function with stdin closed, so it is safe to concatenate after another script over SSH.
 - `network/finding-kb.json`: a **finding knowledge base** keyed by classifier `rule_id` — a remediation entry (category, title, why, read-only *how-to-test* commands, *how-to-fix* steps, references) for every one of the 199 non-low built-in rule_ids. Loaded by `network/report.py` (`_load_finding_kb`, env override `ARANUM_FINDING_KB`); a custom or generic-fallback rule falls back to a service→category map. Guidance commands are templates (`<host>`/`<port>`/`<service>`/…) and never execute; *test* steps are read-only confirmation only.
 - `network/report.py`: findings now carry additive `category` / `kb_id` / `kb_match` (`"rule"` | `"service-default"` | `""`) attached at finalize time, and reports gain a **"Top risks by category"** section grouping non-low findings by KB category and class with their Why / How-to-test / How-to-fix / References. The smb relay-vs-fileservice split keys a host's category on whether it also exposes Kerberos (88) or LDAP (389).
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@ See `CLAUDE.md` §6 for the entry style guide.
 ### Security
 - `network/report.py`: `_load_finding_kb()` now normalizes nested KB structure — category values must be dicts, a class must point at a known category and has its `title`/`why`/`test`/`fix`/`refs` coerced to safe types — so a syntactically valid but structurally malformed KB (a null category, `"test": null`, a class with no title) can never reach a renderer and raise. The "Top risks" section flattens newlines and escapes angle brackets in every interpolated title/why/label/fix-text and renders commands in a backtick-safe inline-code span, so an override KB or an engagement-derived finding title cannot forge a report heading, inject raw HTML, or break out of a code span.
 - `network/report-dashboard.py`: the Active Directory and Categories renderers read finding fields defensively (missing `host`/`line`/`severity` no longer crash rendering), and `_dc_hosts()` coerces numeric string ports so a domain controller is still detected when inventory ports arrive as strings.
+- `network/report.py`: `--redact` matches known hostnames case-insensitively and maps every case variant of a name to one `<TARGET-N>` token (before, `HOST01` survived when the known name was `host01`).
 
 ### Changed
 - `network/report.py`: findings now carry additive `scope` (`"endpoint"` | `"host"` | `"run"`) and structured `host`/`port`/`protocol` attribution fields; the output schema stays `"2"` (purely additive, no consumer break).
